  "airline": "DAL",
  "name": "Team USA Milano Cortina 2026",
  "kind": "special",
  "confidence": "low",
  "drawnOn": "A359",
  "description": "Fuselage: White forward with a red sweep along the lower forward fuselage from under the radome to the wing and a thin navy belly line; from the wing aft the whole fuselage is a gradient running crimson, violet, royal blue (brightest azure low down under the title) to dark navy at the tail, with 26 white stripes (13 a side) converging on the tail cone. Tail: Delta's standard navy fin with the red and dark-red widget. Winglets: navy with a red facet. Titles: 'DELTA' with the widget forward, 'OFFICIAL AIRLINE OF TEAM USA' below it with two US flags and the Olympic and Paralympic marks; huge white 'TEAM USA' aft of the wing. Colors hex: approximate; Delta says over 72 paint colors were used for the gradient and lines.",
